  "result": "The read-only lock is implemented as specified. Typecheck is clean and the existing suite passes (617 tests); no visible test encoded behaviour that changed, so none were edited, and I did not add new tests for the lock itself.\n\nThree things you might not expect:\n\n- **Action-layer gap:** the `create-comment`, `create-issue` and `move-issue` actions run their own rate-limit, quota or feature-flag checks before reaching the service. On a locked workspace those can fire first, so the caller may see that refusal instead of the lock, and a comment attempt still uses up rate-limit allowance. Nothing is written either way. I left them alone because their action-level permission check is looser than the service's, so locking there could change a refusal someone gets today.\n- **Extra action checks:** I added the lock check directly in the `toggle-flag`, `create-webhook`, `create-project` and `invite-member` actions, so their pre-service checks cannot mask the lock.\n- **No banner yet:** `OrganizationSummary.lockReason` is populated, but I did not add the banner to the shell UI.",
